const HELP_HTML=`<div class="panel"><h3>Quick start</h3><ol><li>Press <b>+ Synth track</b> or <b>+ Drum track</b>, then double-click the track lane to add a pattern. Edit it in Piano Roll or Drum Machine.</li><li>To record your voice or guitar, add an audio track, press <b>R</b> on it, then the red <b>Rec</b> button. Tap once to allow the mic. Record over the same spot again to make another take, then pick the best take in the clip panel.</li><li>Add effects in <b>Mixer and FX</b>, or search the <b>Tools Browser</b>.</li><li>Master and export in <b>Mastering</b> and <b>Export and Project</b>.</li></ol>
<h3>Keyboard shortcuts</h3><ul class="cols"><li>Space: play or pause</li><li>Home or Enter: back to start</li><li>R: record</li><li>L: loop on or off</li><li>M: metronome</li><li>S: split selected clip at the playhead</li><li>Delete: delete selected clip</li><li>Ctrl+C, Ctrl+V: copy and paste a clip at the playhead</li><li>Ctrl+D: duplicate clip</li><li>Ctrl+Z, Ctrl+Y: undo and redo</li><li>Ctrl+S: save in browser</li><li>+ and -: zoom</li><li>1 to 9: switch tabs</li><li>Z to M row: play notes (when computer keys are on)</li></ul>
<h3>Honest limits</h3><ul><li>Everything runs in your browser. Very big projects can be slow on phones and older tablets.</li><li>Recording latency depends on your device. Use the latency fix in Settings if takes land late.</li><li>The vocal tuner, harmonizer and pitch shifter are simple real-time designs. They work best on clean solo voice.</li><li>Time-stretch, noise reduction, de-reverb and key detection are basic versions, good for everyday work, not forensic repair.</li><li>Loudness readings are close to LUFS but not certified meters.</li><li>Inside the itch.io page, the mic and MIDI only work if the browser allows them in the embedded frame. If not, open the game in its own window.</li><li>Looping playback restarts with a tiny gap at the loop point.</li><li>Video export saves MP4 where the browser supports it, otherwise WebM.</li></ul></div>`;
function FEATURES_HTML(){ const fx=Object.values(FXDEF).map(d=>d.n).join(', '),ins=Object.values(INSTDEF).map(d=>d.n).join(', ');
 return `<div class="panel"><h3>Everything in Coffeebreak Studio Espresso</h3><ul class="feat"><li><b>Arrange:</b> unlimited audio, synth and drum tracks, clips, snap grid, tempo, time signature, tempo map, markers, loop region, automation lanes for volume, pan and every effect setting, group buses, two FX return buses with sends, freeze and bounce.</li>
 <li><b>Piano roll and drum machine:</b> draw, move, resize and delete notes, velocity strip, quantise with strength, transpose, legato, step sequencer with accents, swing, 5 kits, 14 genre patterns, Surprise me.</li>
 <li><b>MIDI:</b> MIDI keyboard input, on-screen and computer keyboard, MIDI recording, MIDI FX: ${Object.values(MIDIFX_DEF).join(', ')}.</li>
 <li><b>Instruments (${Object.keys(INSTDEF).length} engines, ${Object.keys(INST_PRESETS).length} presets):</b> ${ins}. Named sounds include piano, electric piano, strings, pads, bass, 808, pluck, harp, organs, bells and brass.</li>
 <li><b>Effects (${Object.keys(FXDEF).length}, plus ${fxPresets().length} presets):</b> ${fx}.</li>
 <li><b>Mixer:</b> channel strips with meters, faders, pan, sends, mute, solo, insert chains with bypass and reordering, EQ graph, sidechain ducking from any track.</li>
 <li><b>Recording:</b> several inputs at once, punch in and out, count-in, metronome, input monitoring, takes per clip with comping.</li>
 <li><b>Audio editor:</b> waveform editing, cut, copy, paste, delete, trim, silence, fades, crossfades, time-stretch that keeps pitch, pitch shift that keeps length, reverse, normalise, gain, mono, noise reduction, de-ess, gate, click and pop repair, de-reverb lite.</li>
 <li><b>Mastering:</b> ${Object.keys(MPRE).length} presets, 3-band compression, EQ, stereo width, limiter, loudness targeting, live mastering preview, loudness meter with history, spectrum analyser, spectrogram, phase scope, stereo correlation meter, reference track A/B with level matching.</li>
 <li><b>Tools:</b> tuner with A=432, 440 or 442 and reference tone, chord and scale helper with ${Object.keys(SCALES).length} scales, BPM tap, key and tempo detection, lyric pad with rhyme finder, karaoke mode with vocal reducer, lyrics (plain or LRC), mic chain, and performance recording.</li>
 <li><b>Tools Browser:</b> search over ${buildLib().length} tools, effects, instruments, presets and generators (chord progressions, melodies, drum patterns, arpeggios).</li>
 <li><b>Export:</b> WAV 16, 24 and 32-bit float, MP3, stems per track, video, project save and load in the browser, project files to share or back up.</li>
 <li><b>Comfort:</b> 6 themes, keyboard shortcuts, undo and redo, help, works on desktop and tablet, phone usable, works inside the itch.io page.</li></ul></div>`; }
